harbour-snapszer (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Your own tricks can be looked at: tap your pile of won cards.
  * New setting "Put the trick away by tapping": the finished trick stays
    on the table until you tap it (two, three and four players).
  * The opponent's card points are no longer shown during the hand, as at
    a real table; your own stay, the game points of the match too.
  * A declared 20 or 40 is shown on the table with the second card of
    the pair, as the declarer would show it.
  * The trump card under the talon sticks out further.
  * Rules checked against pagat.com and the Austrian rules: closing the
    talon is no longer allowed when only one face-down card lies on the
    trump (the exchange still is); strict play after closing was right.
  * The opponent's first trick may be looked at, as the soft rules allow:
    tap his pile.

 -- Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200

harbour-snapszer (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Play against another phone over Bluetooth, next to the LAN: hosting opens
    an RFCOMM channel as well, and the join list shows the paired devices.
    Pair the two phones once in the system settings; no network is needed.

